      "content": "It is exhausting to feel trapped in a narrative of mediocrity, but choosing not to \"grind\" isn't the only way to win that race; there are many other tracks for meaningful achievement that don't require a top 0.1% rank. Remember that the people who \"move the world\" often spend years in unnoticed, foundational roles before their impact finally becomes visible, rather than existing only at their peak. Your perspective on value is distorted by the extreme filter of competitive programming scores, which happens to favor a tiny fraction of people on one specific playground.",
